year ago, Thailand granted long-staying refugees from Myanmar the right to work legally. Refugees and rights groups welcome the move but say the program's first year has exposed significant shortcomings.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>From delivery driver to global fame: A Korean writer's journey</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e1ff8308a0542919b6469c5480929233dc612a4477af50af5480977729a6860</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:10:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T10:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/from-delivery-driver-to-global-fame-a-korean-writer-s-journey/a-79672757--a579002c20b4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/from-delivery-driver-to-global-fame-a-korean-writer-s-journey/a-79672757?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">You Yeong-Gwang's The Rainfall Market tells the story of a mysterious, hidden shop that only opens when it rains. For a debut novel by an unknown author, it was a massive success.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: CJP alleges 'deliberate' delay in leaders' release</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:777b5c0f0be873b4135628a0cc532da191d5325621d865bccb5200329091457e</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:10:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T06:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-cjp-alleges-deliberate-delay-in-leaders-release/live-79695410--74850181e334.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-cjp-alleges-deliberate-delay-in-leaders-release/live-79695410?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">CJP leaders Saurav Das and Ashutosh Ranka were due to be released on Sunday. The judge in the case has recused himself after claiming that he was threatened.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Vietnam signs free trade deal with four European countries</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c60a1c65795118e172ee96733fc5557a4914ab4b88728b6b9253c810cb121cb9</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:10:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T09:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/vietnam-signs-free-trade-deal-with-four-european-countries/a-79691812--7e41481b6a6a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/vietnam-signs-free-trade-deal-with-four-european-countries/a-79691812?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Vietnam has signed a deal with four non-EU members that covers trade in goods and services, intellectual property rights, and sustainable development, among other areas.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India: CJP leader Abhijeet Dipke released after detention</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9abed3921b9b1063fd1ebcb88f954e8faf26690a097005e3e222db2e9590c5cb</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:10:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T06:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-cjp-leader-abhijeet-dipke-released-after-detention/a-79690933--80500fd3a662.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-cjp-leader-abhijeet-dipke-released-after-detention/a-79690933?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two other prominent CJP leaders are set to be released on Sunday. India has seen huge rallies calling on the country's top election official to step down over alleged manipulation of voter rolls.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Kolkata stampede dampens Durga Puja festivities</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:db1214db312fe2c4d3d377829fe08214cc8430f5104d31bb83f70f9ac15f358c</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:10:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T04:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-kolkata-stampede-dampens-durga-puja-festivities/live-79685143--9e78a7d0cccd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-kolkata-stampede-dampens-durga-puja-festivities/live-79685143?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Authorities have detained several people over a deadly stampede in India's eastern city of Kolkata, after the state vowed strict action. Meanwhile, 'Cockroach' leader Dipke is out of detention.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>The murder of a young mother in Iran has once again sparked debate on femicide and the social acceptance of violence against women.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3395a6f7ae2eb314e43f152300bd809e9220b47361399978557772fa4a1da7b3</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:10:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T14:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-murder-of-a-young-mother-in-iran-has-once-again-sparked-debate-on-femicide-and-the-social-accept/a-79681977--0dbaaaebbc74.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-murder-of-a-young-mother-in-iran-has-once-again-sparked-debate-on-femicide-and-the-social-acceptance-of-violence-against-women/a-79681977?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The murder of a young mother has once again sparked debate in Iran over so-called honor killings, the social acceptance of violence against women and the lack of protection for people vulnerable to gender-based violence.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India faces water and power shortages after weak monsoon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f547f8791b1d1018463d56a90efd9b4239bf38826a14bbfb242f057f211f28dc</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:10:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T14:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-faces-water-and-power-shortages-after-weak-monsoon/a-79599540--3ab74afcb33c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-faces-water-and-power-shortages-after-weak-monsoon/a-79599540?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A weak monsoon in India is hitting farmers, water supplies and the power system, while raising wider questions about increasingly erratic rainfall and the economic costs.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea warns of AI-aided hacking after bank data breaches</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec0425816692f33c7a0a7519e05a1b190bae9f131963cc8a7093a63f608bc804</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:10:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T12:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-warns-of-ai-aided-hacking-after-bank-data-breaches/a-79592922--3290ee11faa1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-warns-of-ai-aided-hacking-after-bank-data-breaches/a-79592922?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Seoul is alarmed after a recent breach of South Korean banks' cyber defenses that reportedly involved AI-assisted hacking. Officials warn such methods could be used to also target other sectors and government agencies.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>A brutal assault reignites fears over women's safety in India</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe7f6cb5bce7aa02fc3277cd12dcece65f8de19777b343b0a9a88a31a7bc8a45</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:10:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T17:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/a-brutal-assault-reignites-fears-over-women-s-safety-in-india/a-79501471--bceecddefb45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/a-brutal-assault-reignites-fears-over-women-s-safety-in-india/a-79501471?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A string of sexual violence cases has revived questions about women's safety in India, fueling fear, protests and demands for action.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Lawyer of Junaid Hafeez, a Pakistai scholar imprisoned for 13 years, is hopeful for his release</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec738f833b1fd8d2a5c5a937420b44296756c09e9a3650d95343aee5a0bdb032</id><updated>2026-10-19T21:10:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/lawyer-of-junaid-hafeez-a-pakistai-scholar-imprisoned-for-13-years-is-hopeful-for-his-release/a-79490207--6c93b577eab6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/lawyer-of-junaid-hafeez-a-pakistai-scholar-imprisoned-for-13-years-is-hopeful-for-his-release/a-79490207?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A former Fulbright scholar, Junaid Hafeez was sentenced to death under Pakistan's controversial blasphemy laws. His family and lawyer told DW there is now hope a court will overturn the conviction.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
